  <text>
    <body>
      <p>The Carlton Brewery dominated this corner of Carlton for most of the period the directories cover. It is first listed at No. 24 <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref> in 1866, under J. Bellman and Co., and from 1867 under Edward Latham &amp; Co., who also had a brewery in <ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Street">Victoria Street</ref> and stables in <ref target="civic?id=Ballarat%20Street">Ballarat Street</ref>. In 1885 the Bouverie and Victoria Street premises were listed as the Melbourne Brewing and Malting Co., with Latham as manager. In 1890 the Bouverie Street listing still used that name, with Thos. L. Parker as manager, while Victoria Street had become the Carlton &amp; West End Breweries. From 1900 they were the Carlton Brewery Ltd and from 1910 Carlton &amp; United Breweries, spreading over <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref>, <ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Street">Victoria Street</ref>, <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref>, <ref target="civic?id=Ballarat%20Street">Ballarat Street</ref>, <ref target="civic?id=Ballarat%20Lane">Ballarat Lane</ref> and <ref target="civic?id=Swanston%20Street">Swanston Street</ref>. T. L. Parker is listed as manager from 1890 to 1915.</p>
      <p>The directories print the brewery under many names and at many addresses. Each name and place has its own entry, listed below, so that the listings can be followed without merging them. Most of these entries haven't been written yet; <ref target="civic?id=Carlton%20Brewery">Carlton Brewery</ref> is the place to start.</p>
